patch type="changed" "Rooms now use a single peer connection for both publishing and subscribing by default, matching client-sdk-js and rust-sdks. This is what lets the publisher offer ride along with the JOIN request, removing one offer/answer round trip from connect. Servers older than LiveKit OSS 1.9.2 do not serve `/rtc/v1`; the existing fallback re-runs the connect against the legacy path, so the cost there is one failed request rather than a failed connect. Pass `RoomOptions(singlePeerConnection: false)` to keep two peer connections"
